  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{lr}-2, & -2 \\leq x \\leq 0 \\\\ x-2, & 0 < x \\leq 2\\end{array}\\right.$ and $h(x)=f(|x|)+|f(x)|$. Then $\\int_{-2}^2 h(x) \\mathrm{d} x$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "6",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0035_6bf5de49559d.png\"><br><img src=\"assets\\st0035_8dbe012841fc.png\"><br />$h(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{cc}x-2+2-x=0, & 0 \\leq x \\leq 2 \\\\ -x-2+2=-x & -2 \\leq x < 0\\end{array}\\right.$<img src=\"assets\\st0035_362e463eb658.png\"><br />$\\Rightarrow \\int_0^2 \\mathrm{~h}(\\mathrm{x}) \\mathrm{dx}=0$ and $\\int_{-2}^0 \\mathrm{~h}(\\mathrm{x}) \\mathrm{dx}=2$"
  }
}